==German==
{{wikipedia|dab=Ohrwurm (Begriffsklärung)|lang=de}}

===Etymology===
{{compound|Ohr|gloss1=ear|Wurm|gloss2=worm|lang=de}}. In ancient times, dried and ground animals of the order Dermaptera were used to treat ear diseases, which resulted in the Late Latin name {{term|auricula|lang=la}}. Later the name was in error explained as 'worm that enters the ear'.

===Noun===
{{de-noun|g=m|genitive=Ohrwurms|genitive2=Ohrwurmes|plural=Ohrwürmer}}

# [[earwig]], any insect of the order [[Dermaptera]]
# [[earworm]], a tune that pops up in one's memory all of the time

